<task id="017" project="email-communication-solution-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Central-auth alignment + per-rung tests + direction-symmetry tests (inbound == outbound)</title>
    <phase>Wave 1 — Server: enrichment + deterministic engine</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>7</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>012, 013, 014, 015</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, testing</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies `tests/**` and touches auth wiring across the W1 engine surface — TEST-MODIFYING override makes code-review + adr-check UNCONDITIONAL (CLAUDE.md §8); enforces ADR-028 central-auth (no `new` credential) and the direction-symmetry invariant that is the load-bearing correctness guarantee of the whole engine.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W1-tests</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>NFR-03, NFR-06, NFR-08</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close out Wave 1 with the cross-cutting auth + test obligations:

    • **Central-auth alignment (NFR-03/ADR-028)** — audit every W1 service (enrichment, engine, rungs 0–3, status/auto-file, channel seams) and ensure they inject central `TokenCredential` / `IGraphClientFactory` (`ForApp`/`ForUserAsync`) / canonical Dataverse interfaces; **never** `new` a credential or `ConfidentialClientApplication`. Fix any violation found.
    • **Per-rung tests** — a test suite exercising each rung (0,1,2,3) independently: match/no-match, confidence band, provenance recorded, correct target entity.
    • **Direction-symmetry tests** — for equivalent inbound and outbound envelopes, the engine produces IDENTICAL treatment (same matches, same confidence, same status, same provenance) — this is the load-bearing invariant of the whole R4 design.

    Place tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`, and add vertical-slice-seam tests in `tests/integration/seam/**` where the enrichment→engine→status path is a dispatch-spine seam (ADR-038). Follow ADR-038 KEEP-path categories; ban `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, and ctor null-check tests.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF test + auth engineer. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/` and the `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + `tests/integration/seam/**` suites. Fluent in ADR-028 (central auth), ADR-038 (testing strategy — KEEP-path categories, mock-boundary bans, `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice category), ADR-032 (Null-Object), and `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F test obligation.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every W1 Communication service injects central auth (no `new` credential/`ConfidentialClientApplication` anywhere in the W1 surface). A per-rung test suite covers rungs 0–3 (match/no-match, confidence band, provenance, target). A direction-symmetry suite proves inbound and outbound envelopes get identical engine treatment. Dispatch-spine seam tests live in `tests/integration/seam/**`. All tests follow ADR-038 KEEP-path categories and avoid the banned mock boundaries. Build + full test suite green; publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Wave 1 built enrichment (010), the engine (011), rungs 0–3 (012–014), and the status/auto-file ladder (015). Each task authored its own focused tests, but two cross-cutting obligations need a dedicated closing task: (1) NFR-03 central-auth alignment across the whole W1 surface (a single audit + fix pass catches any `new`-credential drift the OOB-email retirement in W0 also targeted), and (2) the direction-symmetry invariant — the single most important correctness guarantee in R4, since the entire premise is that inbound and outbound get identical treatment through one engine.

      ADR-038 governs: tests belong to the 7 KEEP-path categories; `tests/integration/seam/**` is the vertical-slice-seam category (DoD for dispatch-spine changes) — the enrichment→engine→status flow is exactly such a spine, so its end-to-end behavior gets a seam test. Ban `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, and ctor null-check tests.

      This is a TEST-MODIFYING task: per CLAUDE.md §8 the override row makes code-review + adr-check UNCONDITIONAL regardless of default rigor.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingAssociationResolver.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/*.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/*.cs</file>
      <file>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/</file>
      <file>tests/integration/seam/</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">Server injects central `TokenCredential` + `IGraphClientFactory` (`ForApp`/`ForUserAsync`) + canonical Dataverse interfaces; NEVER `new` a credential or `ConfidentialClientApplication`. Audit + fix the whole W1 surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">PRs modifying `Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/` add/update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`; unconditionally-mapped endpoints have unconditional service registration (ADR-032 Null-Object for feature-gated).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Direction-symmetry: equivalent inbound and outbound envelopes MUST produce identical matches, confidence, status, and provenance — assert this explicitly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests follow the 7 KEEP-path categories; add `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam tests for the enrichment→engine→status dispatch spine; BAN `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration tests, ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Per-rung coverage for rungs 0–3: match/no-match, confidence band, provenance recorded, correct target entity. De-duplicate against tests already written in 012–014 (extend/consolidate, don't clone).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">Feature-gated services (e.g. auto-file kill-switch) use Null-Object so unconditional consumers stay registered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta (baseline ~49.63 MB incl. PDBs); no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

