    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Central-auth injection" location=".claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md">
        Inject `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`/canonical Dataverse interfaces; grep the W1 surface for `new ConfidentialClientApplication`/`new ClientSecretCredential` and eliminate.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Direction-symmetry assertion" location="projects/email-communication-solution-r4/notes/011-resolver-behavior-contract.md">
        Build equivalent inbound/outbound `NormalizedMessage` fixtures and assert identical engine output (matches/confidence/status/provenance).
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Vertical-slice seam test" location="docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md">
        `tests/integration/seam/**` exercises the enrichment→engine→status spine end-to-end (real wiring, boundary fakes only) as the DoD for dispatch-spine changes.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Grep the W1 Communication surface for `new ConfidentialClientApplication`, `new ClientSecretCredential`, `new DefaultAzureCredential`, and token-snapshot patterns; list any violations.</step>
    <step order="2">Fix each violation: inject central `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`/canonical Dataverse interfaces via constructor (ADR-028). Register via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010), unconditional.</step>
    <step order="3">Read ADR-038 + `tests/CLAUDE.md` + `TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md` to confirm KEEP-path categories, the mock-boundary bans, and the `tests/integration/seam/**` category before writing tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Inventory tests already written by 012/013/014/015; consolidate/extend into a coherent per-rung suite (rungs 0–3: match/no-match, confidence band, provenance, target entity) — do not clone.</step>
    <step order="5">Author the direction-symmetry suite: for a set of scenarios, build equivalent inbound + outbound `NormalizedMessage` fixtures and assert identical engine output (matches, confidence, status, provenance). Cover at least one scenario per rung + the auto-file/kill-switch path.</step>
    <step order="6">Add `tests/integration/seam/**` vertical-slice-seam tests exercising the enrichment→engine→status spine end-to-end (real wiring; only boundary fakes; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + full `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + `dotnet test tests/integration/seam/`; confirm all green, including 011 characterization + 012–015 tests.</step>
    <step order="7.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o c:/tmp/r4-017-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0.</step>
    <step order="7.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL / TEST-MODIFYING quality gates (UNCONDITIONAL): `code-review` on the diff; `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus NFR-03 central-auth + NFR-08 test obligation + ADR-038 KEEP-path + direction-symmetry). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (017 ✅) + `current-task.md`; note that Wave 1 is complete; record decisions (symmetry fixture strategy, seam-test scope, any auth fixes made).</step>
  </steps>

