  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">No `new ConfidentialClientApplication` / `new *Credential` in the W1 Communication surface (grep-clean); all services inject central `TokenCredential`/`IGraphClientFactory`/canonical Dataverse interfaces (NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A per-rung suite covers rungs 0–3: match/no-match, confidence band, provenance recorded, correct target entity.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A direction-symmetry suite proves equivalent inbound and outbound envelopes yield identical matches, confidence, status, and provenance.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Vertical-slice-seam tests exist in `tests/integration/seam/**` for the enrichment→engine→status dispatch spine (real wiring, boundary fakes only).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All tests follow ADR-038 KEEP-path categories; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or ctor null-check tests are added.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full `dotnet test` (unit + seam) green, including 011 characterization + 012–015 tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    TEST-MODIFYING rigor override (CLAUDE.md §8): code-review + adr-check are UNCONDITIONAL here regardless of the default STANDARD-skip — this task modifies `tests/**` and carries the `testing` tag.

    De-duplicate rather than clone: 012–015 already wrote focused tests; this task consolidates them into coherent per-rung + symmetry suites and adds the seam-level coverage they could not (cross-task, end-to-end).

    Direction symmetry is THE load-bearing R4 invariant — if any scenario is asymmetric, that is a real bug in 010/011/012–015, not a test to weaken; escalate and fix the source.
  </notes>

